1
00:01:44,720 --> 00:01:45,560
Dad.

2
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:50,480
Would you be mad at me like Ob?

3
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:54,200
I'm so sorry.

4
00:01:55,040 --> 00:01:56,680
There really was no other way.

5
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:23,320
"Today we welcomed Hom Thong,
our newest family member."

6
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:25,600
Auem.

7
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:26,520
Here.

8
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:28,440
Thanks, dear.

9
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:32,560
You can sleep inside, you know?

10
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:34,960
You're gonna hurt your back sleeping here.

11
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:40,120
Hom Ngern had a miscarriage before.

12
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:44,480
If Hom Thong comes out
as perfect as I'm hoping,

13
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:47,040
I'll give him the best life.

14
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:49,840
You already named Hom Ngern's baby?

15
00:02:49,920 --> 00:02:51,160
Yeah, of course.

16
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:54,920
Mom's Hom Ngern. The baby's Hom Thong.

17
00:02:55,680 --> 00:03:00,320
I'll enter him in competitions
and make a name for our farm.

18
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:03,120
So I can open
a buffalo conservation center

19
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:05,080
like I've dreamed of.

20
00:03:08,440 --> 00:03:13,640
Go tell Ob to go get the vet!
Hom Thong's coming! Go!

21
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:16,280
-Go on, quick!
-Okay, Dad.

22
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:17,480
Tell Ob to get the vet!

23
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:28,000
"Today, Hom Thong saved Auem like a hero."

24
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:35,040
Hello, Dad. I don't know,
something's wrong with my car.

25
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:38,560
I'm at Ta Daeng's store.

26
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:41,040
Okay. Please come as soon as you can.

27
00:03:43,080 --> 00:03:44,640
Hello, hello.

28
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:47,440
Hi there. Can we help you?

29
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:53,920
Your car broke down?
Should we fix it for you?

30
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,240
No, thanks. My dad's on his way.

31
00:03:56,320 --> 00:03:59,640
Let's not bother your dad.
It's no big deal.

32
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:02,040
We can take care of it, no problem.

33
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:04,800
Geez!

34
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:09,440
Hom Thong?

35
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:11,400
Oh, Auem?

36
00:04:14,320 --> 00:04:16,160
No wonder Hom Thong suddenly ran off.

37
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:18,360
He was following your voice.

38
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:40,360
Right, you must be hungry. Here you go.

39
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:43,200
Eat up.

40
00:04:44,880 --> 00:04:47,920
Here you go.

41
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:53,800
Din.

42
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:56,720
I need your help with something.

43
00:04:58,280 --> 00:05:00,080
You're getting Hom Thong back?

44
00:05:01,920 --> 00:05:02,960
How did you know?

45
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:04,760
Someone like you

46
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:07,560
could never bring yourself
to hurt your family.

47
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:11,120
You're Uncle Yod's daughter.

48
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:24,360
Let's go get Hom Thong back.

49
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:34,520
DRIVE
2 HOURS 38 MINUTES

50
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:38,840
HEAD NORTHEAST
TURN RIGHT

51
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:40,080
Whoa, Auem.

52
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:43,800
It's two and a half hours
to Uthai Thani from Ayutthaya.

53
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:49,440
I'll get Hom Thong back,
even if it takes ten hours to get there.

54
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:51,520
Thanks, Auem.

55
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:59,200
UTHAI THANI PROVINCE

56
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:04,480
Here's one million baht.
I'd like to buy Hom Thong back.

57
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,360
Why do you want him back all of a sudden?

58
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:12,720
I was too hasty then.
I didn't think it through.

59
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:16,520
I forgot how much
Dad and Ob love Hom Thong.

60
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:21,280
Please, Sia Aun. You already have
a lot of nice buffaloes.

61
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:23,240
Your Racha Uthai just won so many prizes.

62
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:25,320
Please let me have Hom Thong back.

63
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:29,680
Sure.

64
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:33,760
I'll give it back to you, but…

65
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:36,160
not for a million.

66
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:39,960
What do you mean?

67
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:44,600
What? It's not like you're new
to the show buffalo scene.

68
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:49,560
Buying and selling buffaloes
is really up to their owners.

69
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:51,760
And I'm Hom Thong's owner now.

70
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:57,520
If you want him back,
I'll need two million.

71
00:06:58,600 --> 00:06:59,680
What?

72
00:06:59,760 --> 00:07:02,800
You're doubling the price
after just one day?

73
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:05,760
You're playing dirty.
Give me back my buffalo.

74
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:09,800
Hey, hey. What are you people on about?

75
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:13,280
He bought that buffalo fair and square.
No money? Go home then.

76
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:14,920
Hey, kick them out!

77
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:16,880
-Come on.
-Hey!

78
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:18,560
-What are you doing? Let go!
-Leave!

79
00:07:18,640 --> 00:07:20,080
-Get out!
-Let go of me!

80
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:21,680
-Let go!
-Are you gonna leave?

81
00:07:21,760 --> 00:07:23,120
Let go of me!

82
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:25,720
I won't let you!
Give Hom Thong back to me!

83
00:07:26,400 --> 00:07:29,400
Give me two million, and he's all yours.

84
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:32,160
Auem, you can't just leave Hom Thong here!

85
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:36,320
Fine! I'll buy him back for two million!

86
00:07:41,440 --> 00:07:42,880
Great, just wire me the money.

87
00:07:43,520 --> 00:07:47,040
Are you mad? You know she's in debt.

88
00:07:47,120 --> 00:07:48,520
Give her some time.

89
00:07:50,640 --> 00:07:53,440
Okay. For Yod's sake,

90
00:07:54,360 --> 00:07:57,280
I'll give you six months.

91
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:02,400
One million in six months?
That's a bit too tight, don't you think?

92
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:04,360
If you don't take this deal,

93
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:05,320
then just forget it.

94
00:08:15,960 --> 00:08:16,800
Fine.

95
00:08:17,360 --> 00:08:19,840
But it must be put in writing
that in the next six months,

96
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:22,040
you won't sell Hom Thong to anyone.

97
00:08:38,039 --> 00:08:39,360
One copy for each of us.

98
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:44,400
This guarantees I won't sell Hom Thong
to anyone in the next six months

99
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:48,480
until you have the money to buy him back.

100
00:08:49,520 --> 00:08:52,040
In the meantime, I'll come here
to take care of Hom Thong.

101
00:08:52,800 --> 00:08:55,720
You can't do that.
You have to go to school.

102
00:08:55,800 --> 00:08:58,720
And Uthai Thani's miles from Ayutthaya.

103
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:01,600
Well, just on weekends.

104
00:09:01,680 --> 00:09:03,200
I'll take the minibus.

105
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:05,920
I also wanna make sure
that Sia Aun won't try anything.

106
00:09:06,680 --> 00:09:10,240
Don't worry, sis.
I won't let this get in the way of school.

107
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:11,160
Come on, please.

108
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:18,720
I don't mind if Ob's coming here
to take care of Hom Thong.

109
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:23,800
Okay then. In six months,

110
00:09:23,880 --> 00:09:27,040
I'll bring you two million,
and I'll take Hom Thong back with me.

111
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:44,760
Six months? Why so generous?

112
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:48,480
You know how small
the show buffalo business is.

113
00:09:49,440 --> 00:09:54,160
It'll only hurt my reputation
if they post about me bullying them.

114
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:58,360
Their family owes millions.

115
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:02,240
And now they have to find
another million in six months.

116
00:10:04,320 --> 00:10:05,520
I doubt they can do it.

117
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:08,440
But what if they can?

118
00:10:09,680 --> 00:10:14,080
Then let's cash in on Hom Thong's semen
in the next six months.

119
00:10:16,680 --> 00:10:18,800
But now that Hom Thong's ours,

120
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:22,160
there's no way I'll let them

121
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:23,880
get him back just like that.

122
00:10:40,080 --> 00:10:42,600
Eat as much as you can while you're here.

123
00:10:43,360 --> 00:10:44,960
And take good care of yourself.

124
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:49,560
You'll come back to us
in six months, okay?

125
00:10:57,280 --> 00:10:58,480
They just moved him,

126
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:01,880
so he's lost his appetite.
Here, let me help you.

127
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:04,440
But I still don't get it.

128
00:11:05,400 --> 00:11:07,520
Why did you let Ob work at our farm?

129
00:11:08,160 --> 00:11:09,200
Isn't that too risky?

130
00:11:10,040 --> 00:11:14,480
Don't you see that Hom Thong only eats
when Ob's here?

131
00:11:15,560 --> 00:11:16,600
They're very close.

132
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:22,160
If we want to drive up Hom Thong's
market value beyond what we paid,

133
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:25,600
-we must trick the owner to do the work.
-I see.

134
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:29,840
That's how it is. Got it, Sia Aun.

135
00:11:29,920 --> 00:11:31,320
Keep an eye on him.

136
00:11:31,400 --> 00:11:33,360
Don't let him poke his nose elsewhere.

137
00:11:43,880 --> 00:11:46,440
-Mom.
-Come on, faster!

138
00:11:47,040 --> 00:11:49,760
Look, I'll drop you off
at the bus station.

139
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:52,840
You'll go to Bangkok to get a job.

140
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:54,560
You can't quit just like that.

141
00:11:54,640 --> 00:11:56,320
-Mom. Mom.
-What?

142
00:11:56,840 --> 00:12:00,800
-Be reasonable! I did think it through.
-You did?

143
00:12:01,520 --> 00:12:06,360
Come on, how much
can that animal feed store pay you?

144
00:12:06,440 --> 00:12:08,360
But the marketing position Rung got me

145
00:12:08,440 --> 00:12:10,240
pays as much as the job in Bangkok.

146
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:14,240
And if I work here in our hometown,
I can save a lot of money.

147
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:19,720
But right now,
I'm gonna have to cut everyone's pay.

148
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:23,200
Wait, what does my allowance
have to do with this?

149
00:12:23,280 --> 00:12:25,760
I could barely survive
on what Dad gave me.

150
00:12:25,840 --> 00:12:28,240
Orn, we'll all have to live frugally now.

151
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:32,440
If you hadn't given Ob his way
and used the million to pay off the debt,

152
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:34,000
we wouldn't be in this situation.

153
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:39,200
I'm not getting Hom Thong back
to please Ob, you know.

154
00:12:39,280 --> 00:12:41,200
I just wanna keep Dad's buffaloes.

155
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:43,320
And when we pay everything off,

156
00:12:43,400 --> 00:12:45,720
I'm gonna open
a buffalo conservation center.

157
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:46,720
Huh?

158
00:12:46,800 --> 00:12:49,720
Did your dad visit you
in your dream or something?

159
00:12:49,800 --> 00:12:52,200
Even your dad

160
00:12:52,280 --> 00:12:55,800
couldn't make
this buffalo center thing happen.

161
00:12:55,880 --> 00:12:58,040
Then I'm gonna show you that I can.

162
00:12:59,280 --> 00:13:01,760
I'll help you.
I don't want any more allowance.

163
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:04,560
I'll use the money I get
from taking care of Hom Thong.

164
00:13:04,640 --> 00:13:07,640
You just save up,
buy him back as soon as you can,

165
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:09,000
and open the buffalo center.

166
00:13:10,400 --> 00:13:13,840
Do whatever you want.
Just don't touch my money.

167
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:16,040
Listen to her.

168
00:13:21,440 --> 00:13:24,000
Look, I'm warning you
because I care about you.

169
00:13:24,640 --> 00:13:27,560
Don't make things difficult.
You're just gonna get exhausted.

170
00:13:28,400 --> 00:13:29,840
Got it? Here.

171
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:50,160
CAN YOU COME SEE ME AFTER WORK, RUT?

172
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:55,200
You're gonna work at the same place as me?

173
00:13:56,040 --> 00:13:58,720
Yeah, starting next week.

174
00:13:58,800 --> 00:14:00,320
Whoa, Auem. What's going on here?

175
00:14:00,400 --> 00:14:02,640
Why didn't you discuss it with me first?

176
00:14:02,720 --> 00:14:05,280
I did text you,
but you didn't text me back.

177
00:14:05,360 --> 00:14:07,280
I thought you were busy.

178
00:14:07,880 --> 00:14:10,800
So that's it?
That's all you wanna talk to me about?

179
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:14,200
What's wrong with you, Rut?

180
00:14:14,280 --> 00:14:16,720
Aren't you happy that
we're gonna be working together?

181
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:22,920
It's not like that.

182
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:30,560
I just hate to see you
give up your Bangkok job.

183
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:33,720
Fine, whatever.

184
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:36,880
See you at the store, okay?

185
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:39,600
I'm gonna head home now.
My mom's a bit unwell.

186
00:14:40,720 --> 00:14:41,560
Rut.

187
00:14:42,640 --> 00:14:43,480
Well…

188
00:14:46,040 --> 00:14:48,080
About the gold
we've been saving up together,

189
00:14:49,960 --> 00:14:54,480
I want to sell my share now
so I can pay the aunties and uncles back.

190
00:14:56,760 --> 00:14:57,880
Pay them back?

191
00:14:57,960 --> 00:14:59,080
For what?

192
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:02,640
You couldn't cover your debts
with that one million from the buffalo?

193
00:15:03,680 --> 00:15:05,360
I'm trying to get Hom Thong back.

194
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:07,880
And I want to open
a buffalo conservation center for Dad.

195
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:10,240
Wait, what's going on?

196
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:12,160
First the job, now the buffalo.

197
00:15:12,240 --> 00:15:13,400
I'm your boyfriend.

198
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:15,240
How come I'm the last to know?

199
00:15:15,320 --> 00:15:18,120
I would've told you everything
had you answered your phone.

200
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:20,440
Oh, so I'm in the wrong here?
Are you blaming me?

201
00:15:20,520 --> 00:15:21,400
Rut.

202
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:23,240
Fine. Do whatever you want.

203
00:15:23,320 --> 00:15:25,640
Work wherever you want.
Raise buffaloes if you want.

204
00:15:25,720 --> 00:15:27,080
Do whatever you want, okay?

205
00:15:27,800 --> 00:15:28,960
I'm done.

206
00:15:31,120 --> 00:15:32,000
Rut.

207
00:15:50,960 --> 00:15:52,200
Can I sit here, Hom Ngern?

208
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:49,880
How's it going?

209
00:16:52,440 --> 00:16:55,280
I guess you and Ob
are the only ones supporting me.

210
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:58,960
Do you think I can make
Dad's buffalo center a reality?

211
00:16:59,720 --> 00:17:00,840
Yeah?

212
00:17:01,440 --> 00:17:02,920
If I'd listened to Dad more

213
00:17:04,839 --> 00:17:06,880
when he was still alive,

214
00:17:07,720 --> 00:17:11,359
I would've known by now where to start.

215
00:17:30,840 --> 00:17:31,760
Alright.

216
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:35,600
Chop young banana stalks
into small pieces like this.

217
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:39,720
We'll mix the banana stalks
with one part fine rice bran…

218
00:17:41,840 --> 00:17:44,200
and one part soybean meal.

219
00:17:46,400 --> 00:17:49,600
Once everything's in, give it a good mix.

220
00:17:49,680 --> 00:17:52,080
Mix it just like this.

221
00:17:53,160 --> 00:17:54,240
That's right.

222
00:17:54,920 --> 00:17:58,480
Now we have
a nutritional supplement for buffaloes.

223
00:17:58,560 --> 00:18:02,840
This works wonders on pregnant buffaloes.
They'll be even healthier.

224
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:06,120
Oh, I want my buffaloes
to have shinier coats.

225
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:07,840
What do I feed them, Din?

226
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:08,960
Wow.

227
00:18:09,040 --> 00:18:10,600
Great question from Uncle Toi here.

228
00:18:11,240 --> 00:18:15,720
Roughly grind some raw sunflower seeds
and mix them with fine rice bran.

229
00:18:15,800 --> 00:18:19,640
Or you can mix sunflower seed meal
with concentrated feed.

230
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:23,960
The healthy fats in sunflower seeds
will keep buffaloes' coats shiny.

231
00:18:26,960 --> 00:18:28,600
Uh, any more questions?

232
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:33,920
What do I have to do for you
to teach me how to raise buffaloes?

233
00:18:52,640 --> 00:18:53,560
Hey, Auem.

234
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:57,480
Why this urge to raise buffaloes
all of a sudden?

235
00:18:58,360 --> 00:19:00,640
I wanna make some extra money.

236
00:19:00,720 --> 00:19:02,200
I already did some calculations.

237
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:04,200
I have to earn one million in six months.

238
00:19:04,280 --> 00:19:07,320
That means I have to earn
around 100,000 baht a month.

239
00:19:07,400 --> 00:19:10,560
There's no way I can get that
from just one full-time job.

240
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:13,880
So you wanna earn
some extra income with Hom Ngern?

241
00:19:14,480 --> 00:19:16,920
Yeah, and I need your help.

242
00:19:17,520 --> 00:19:20,960
Well, I wanna know Buffalo Raising 101.

243
00:19:22,520 --> 00:19:23,840
Hmm.

244
00:19:23,920 --> 00:19:29,680
I wonder if a buffalo farmer like me
can teach you anything.

245
00:19:31,080 --> 00:19:32,440
Come on, Din.

246
00:19:32,520 --> 00:19:34,760
I'm sorry about what I said.

247
00:19:35,720 --> 00:19:39,600
But right now,
you're the only one I can rely on.

248
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:46,120
If you're still mad at me,

249
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:48,320
just tell me what you want me to do.

250
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:50,600
Anything. I'll do it.

251
00:19:51,840 --> 00:19:53,240
Please, Din?

252
00:19:58,120 --> 00:20:02,160
Are you sure that you'd do anything?

253
00:20:16,800 --> 00:20:18,040
Ah!

254
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:27,040
I'm done scooping up
the buffalo dung. What next?

255
00:20:27,840 --> 00:20:29,160
Dry the dung in the sun.

256
00:20:35,840 --> 00:20:37,680
Do you know what buffalo dung's good for?

257
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:39,240
Fertilizer.

258
00:20:39,320 --> 00:20:40,840
1. ORGANIC FERTILIZER

259
00:20:40,920 --> 00:20:42,520
Aside from that,

260
00:20:43,360 --> 00:20:46,640
you can mix buffalo dung
with water and strong-smelling herbs

261
00:20:47,240 --> 00:20:48,480
to make an insect repellent.

262
00:20:49,080 --> 00:20:53,840
Flattened, sun-dried buffalo dung
can be made into charcoal.

263
00:20:53,920 --> 00:20:56,920
If you don't want any hassle,
you can dry the dung in the sun

264
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:58,840
and sell it by the sack
for 30 baht a sack.

265
00:21:13,680 --> 00:21:17,280
Anything else that can give us
some extra income?

266
00:21:17,880 --> 00:21:19,480
When Uncle Yod was here,

267
00:21:19,560 --> 00:21:22,400
he cut and sold the Pangola grass
he grew in the backyard.

268
00:21:22,480 --> 00:21:25,320
-That's 80 baht a bale.
-Okay.

269
00:21:25,400 --> 00:21:27,240
I'll take over cutting the grass.

270
00:21:28,040 --> 00:21:33,360
Oh, Din. Can we enter Hom Ngern
in shows and win prizes like Dad did?

271
00:21:33,440 --> 00:21:36,880
Sure, but you won't get much money.

272
00:21:36,960 --> 00:21:39,440
What you get from competitions
is actually fame.

273
00:21:40,120 --> 00:21:41,560
People will know of our buffalo.

274
00:21:41,640 --> 00:21:45,280
A male buffalo's semen value
will also increase when it wins.

275
00:21:45,360 --> 00:21:49,800
But Hom Ngern's a female.
Most people milk their female buffaloes

276
00:21:49,880 --> 00:21:51,400
and keep them for breeding.

277
00:21:51,480 --> 00:21:53,760
A handsome male
will be used to mate with the females.

278
00:21:53,840 --> 00:21:55,800
Then they wait for the calves
and sell them.

279
00:21:56,960 --> 00:21:57,880
Wow.

280
00:21:58,480 --> 00:22:01,400
Doesn't it take buffaloes
years to give birth?

281
00:22:01,480 --> 00:22:04,400
Isn't there any faster way to get money?

282
00:22:04,480 --> 00:22:06,680
Everything about buffaloes
takes time, Auem.

283
00:22:07,600 --> 00:22:08,640
Geez.

284
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:11,760
How am I gonna make
that much money in time?

285
00:22:11,840 --> 00:22:13,560
We're talking about over 100,000 a month!

286
00:22:14,880 --> 00:22:20,160
Relax, Auem. I'm sure there's a way
to make a quick buck with buffaloes.

287
00:22:21,040 --> 00:22:22,320
I'll help you think of something.

288
00:22:34,360 --> 00:22:37,280
I scooped up the dung.
I even laid it out to dry.

289
00:22:37,360 --> 00:22:39,280
Will you teach me
how to raise buffaloes now?

290
00:22:41,280 --> 00:22:42,640
But I am.

291
00:22:43,840 --> 00:22:47,440
What? Scooping the dung and drying it?

292
00:22:47,520 --> 00:22:49,360
What's it got to do
with raising buffaloes?

293
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:52,200
You know, when I first started,

294
00:22:52,280 --> 00:22:53,960
Uncle Yod made me haul 20 dung barrels!

295
00:22:54,040 --> 00:22:56,840
My hands were all shaky and achy!

296
00:22:56,920 --> 00:22:59,440
Good. He should've made you
haul 100 barrels.

297
00:22:59,520 --> 00:23:02,160
Hey, do you wanna learn from me or what?

298
00:23:02,240 --> 00:23:06,960
Okay, fine. What else
did Dad ask you to do that day?

299
00:23:09,320 --> 00:23:10,960
When I finished scooping the dung,

300
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:14,760
Uncle Yod made me promise

301
00:23:15,920 --> 00:23:19,520
that everything I learned from him
would be passed on.

302
00:23:20,720 --> 00:23:22,320
He'd be so happy to know

303
00:23:22,960 --> 00:23:24,800
that the knowledge he gave me

304
00:23:26,040 --> 00:23:27,240
is now his daughter's.

305
00:23:37,920 --> 00:23:40,080
You're helping me out, Dad?

306
00:23:47,200 --> 00:23:49,280
Rut got that angry at you?

307
00:23:49,960 --> 00:23:53,720
Yeah. He left me on read.

308
00:23:53,800 --> 00:23:56,480
Don't worry. When we see him
at the office next week,

309
00:23:56,560 --> 00:23:58,000
I'll lead the charge!

310
00:23:58,080 --> 00:24:01,920
It's okay, really. I've got a lot
on my plate right now.

311
00:24:03,680 --> 00:24:04,680
Alright.

312
00:24:05,880 --> 00:24:09,200
I've got everything here. Ready to shoot?

313
00:24:09,280 --> 00:24:10,560
Yes.

314
00:24:10,640 --> 00:24:12,040
-Shooting?
-Just follow me.

315
00:24:14,760 --> 00:24:17,360
Shooting a new TikTok star, of course.

316
00:24:17,440 --> 00:24:20,520
Mom saw a vendor at school making videos.

317
00:24:20,600 --> 00:24:22,080
So she asked me to help shoot some.

318
00:24:22,960 --> 00:24:26,120
It's been five months.
I have almost 50,000 followers now.

319
00:24:26,760 --> 00:24:29,520
I add product links to my vids
to make some extra money.

320
00:24:29,600 --> 00:24:31,560
I get almost 10,000 a month!

321
00:24:32,200 --> 00:24:34,520
-Almost 10,000?
-Yeah.

322
00:24:34,600 --> 00:24:38,560
I even got asked
to review some chili paste.

323
00:24:38,640 --> 00:24:41,200
Mae Wandee chili paste or something.

324
00:24:41,280 --> 00:24:43,680
And I got 5,000 just for that.

325
00:24:46,080 --> 00:24:47,960
-Right, hit that button.
-Ready, Mom?

326
00:24:48,040 --> 00:24:49,800
-Yes.
-Here we go.

327
00:24:51,040 --> 00:24:54,400
Hello. Welcome to Kitchen
with Aunt Sa-Ang.

328
00:24:54,480 --> 00:25:00,440
I'll show you how to make an easy,
yummy dish anyone can make.

329
00:25:00,520 --> 00:25:04,640
This is squid laab.

330
00:25:04,720 --> 00:25:06,440
But before we make this spicy dish,

331
00:25:06,520 --> 00:25:11,760
feel free to send me some little gifts.

332
00:25:11,840 --> 00:25:16,360
Aw, thanks!
Thank you for sending me three flowers.

333
00:25:16,440 --> 00:25:21,680
But bigger gifts
will surely make me feel a lot better.

334
00:25:21,760 --> 00:25:25,480
Anything else? Oh, thank you!

335
00:25:25,560 --> 00:25:29,240
A car for me to drive?
Thanks so much for sending that.

336
00:25:29,320 --> 00:25:33,560
-Here's my fresh squid.
-Now I know how to get that extra money.

337
00:25:33,640 --> 00:25:37,120
Give it a quick blanch and set aside.

338
00:25:43,640 --> 00:25:45,360
You're gonna make buffalo content?

339
00:25:46,080 --> 00:25:49,000
Yeah, I'll make TikTok and YouTube videos.

340
00:25:49,080 --> 00:25:51,520
That way, I can pay off my debts
and get Hom Thong back.

341
00:25:52,040 --> 00:25:55,000
But we only have six months.
You sure this is gonna work?

342
00:25:55,080 --> 00:25:58,360
I already talked to Aunt Sa-Ang
and did some research.

343
00:25:58,440 --> 00:26:01,000
Once we have
a thousand followers on TikTok,

344
00:26:01,080 --> 00:26:04,320
we can add product links to our profile.
The more followers we have,

345
00:26:04,400 --> 00:26:06,400
the more reviewing gigs we'll get.

346
00:26:06,480 --> 00:26:09,520
The more reviews, the more monthly income.

347
00:26:09,600 --> 00:26:12,320
Hmm, that's not a bad idea since

348
00:26:12,400 --> 00:26:14,160
Hom Ngern's the mom of a champion.

349
00:26:14,240 --> 00:26:16,320
If we make this our selling point,

350
00:26:16,400 --> 00:26:18,600
Hom Ngern might get hired
for some review gigs.

351
00:26:18,680 --> 00:26:21,600
I can sell Dad's Pangola grass online too.

352
00:26:21,680 --> 00:26:25,640
There's this one buffalo farmer guy.

353
00:26:25,720 --> 00:26:29,160
He makes buffalo supplements.
Everyone buys from him.

354
00:26:29,240 --> 00:26:30,800
-Mm-hm.
-Hmm.

355
00:26:30,880 --> 00:26:32,880
But we'll have to film and upload daily.

356
00:26:32,960 --> 00:26:34,960
Those with product links on their profile

357
00:26:35,040 --> 00:26:38,320
upload 10 to 20 videos a day.
That's how they earn 100,000 a month.

358
00:26:38,400 --> 00:26:41,720
Yeah. If you're making content,
you gotta make it good. Really good.

359
00:26:41,800 --> 00:26:43,560
So you get a big audience.

360
00:26:43,640 --> 00:26:44,720
Exactly.

361
00:26:45,320 --> 00:26:46,880
That's why I need your help.

362
00:26:48,160 --> 00:26:51,680
My content will mostly be about
raising show buffaloes.

363
00:26:51,760 --> 00:26:54,360
Some will be educational, and some

364
00:26:54,440 --> 00:26:57,160
will be cute dance vids
with the buffalo, like Moo Deng vids!

365
00:26:58,280 --> 00:26:59,480
"Don't touch me!"

366
00:27:02,600 --> 00:27:03,960
You sure about that, Auem?

367
00:27:04,040 --> 00:27:05,600
Come on, Din.

368
00:27:08,560 --> 00:27:10,920
Okay, I'll help you.

369
00:27:11,960 --> 00:27:16,000
But what should our first video be?

370
00:27:17,280 --> 00:27:23,120
Hom Ngern, Phetkla, I hired
some pretty boys to bathe you.

371
00:27:23,200 --> 00:27:26,240
Where are they? I wanna meet them.

372
00:27:26,320 --> 00:27:32,080
I wanna meet them too.
I wonder if they're as handsome as me.

373
00:27:32,160 --> 00:27:33,720
You got it.

374
00:27:35,320 --> 00:27:38,240
Dinny, Obby, come on in.

375
00:27:41,920 --> 00:27:43,000
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Wow.</font></font></i>

376
00:27:48,040 --> 00:27:53,080
Dinny, why do us buffaloes
need to take a bath?

377
00:27:54,520 --> 00:27:56,480
Naturally,

378
00:27:56,560 --> 00:28:00,520
buffaloes love soaking in water and mud,
getting all wet and muddy.

379
00:28:00,600 --> 00:28:05,240
They have fewer sweat glands
than other animals.

380
00:28:05,320 --> 00:28:09,080
So they have a harder time cooling down.

381
00:28:09,720 --> 00:28:13,480
You guys get moody
when it gets hot, don't you?

382
00:28:13,560 --> 00:28:19,520
That's right. We get uncomfortable
when we're too hot.

383
00:28:20,560 --> 00:28:25,400
And do you two know that
soaking in water and mud

384
00:28:25,480 --> 00:28:28,280
can protect you from the heat of the sun?

385
00:28:28,360 --> 00:28:31,920
It can really help cool you down.

386
00:28:35,680 --> 00:28:36,800
Let's bathe.

387
00:28:36,880 --> 00:28:40,480
-Does that feel good, Phetkla?
-It does.

388
00:28:44,920 --> 00:28:47,440
ANIMAL FEED STORE

389
00:28:49,960 --> 00:28:53,560
Auem's gonna be working here
in just a few days. What do I do, man?

390
00:28:53,640 --> 00:28:57,640
Why don't you just break up with her
and get it over with?

391
00:28:57,720 --> 00:29:00,960
If I do that now,
she's just gonna ask for her gold.

392
00:29:01,040 --> 00:29:03,080
I already sold all the gold
we've saved up.

393
00:29:03,160 --> 00:29:06,040
Shoot, you're in trouble then.

394
00:29:06,120 --> 00:29:09,240
There's no way she won't find out
when she starts working here.

395
00:29:09,840 --> 00:29:11,120
Thanks for rubbing it in.

396
00:29:12,840 --> 00:29:14,360
-Now what?
-I don't fricking know.

397
00:29:14,440 --> 00:29:16,160
-Oops!
-Ah!

398
00:29:17,680 --> 00:29:18,800
You okay?

399
00:29:19,880 --> 00:29:21,120
I'm okay.

400
00:29:22,840 --> 00:29:23,720
Hey, Rut.

401
00:29:24,880 --> 00:29:26,200
Hi there, Mr. Chettha.

402
00:29:26,280 --> 00:29:30,080
Remember how I asked you
to show my daughter the ropes?

403
00:29:30,160 --> 00:29:31,400
Let's start tomorrow, okay?

404
00:29:32,680 --> 00:29:35,000
Uh, your daughter?

405
00:29:35,080 --> 00:29:37,840
Hi, Rut. I'm Ming.

406
00:29:41,360 --> 00:29:42,280
Hello.

407
00:29:49,480 --> 00:29:52,280
Here's the Pangola grass we grew at home.

408
00:29:52,360 --> 00:29:54,320
Absolutely 100% organic.

409
00:29:54,400 --> 00:29:57,200
If you'd like some of this
for your lovely buffaloes,

410
00:29:57,280 --> 00:30:00,720
please call this number down here.
And look at this.

411
00:30:01,840 --> 00:30:03,000
Hom Ngern!

412
00:30:03,720 --> 00:30:05,200
Eat this.

413
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:07,480
Good girl.

414
00:30:08,080 --> 00:30:10,560
See? Hom Ngern loves it too.

415
00:30:11,240 --> 00:30:15,240
She's not the only buffalo
loving this grass, but Hom Thong too.

416
00:30:15,320 --> 00:30:16,600
Our grass made him a champion.

417
00:30:16,680 --> 00:30:18,800
If you want your buffaloes
to win prizes too,

418
00:30:18,880 --> 00:30:21,840
then the only grass for you
is Por Yod's Pangola grass.

419
00:30:22,440 --> 00:30:25,360
Feel free to order now. We've got plenty.

420
00:30:25,440 --> 00:30:27,320
That's right,
and they're ready to ship out.

421
00:30:27,400 --> 00:30:30,320
Please, Mom. Buy this for me.

422
00:30:30,400 --> 00:30:33,080
It's not like he's here every day.

423
00:30:33,160 --> 00:30:35,880
-Please, Mom. Buy me one.
-I already told you.

424
00:30:35,960 --> 00:30:39,280
-I made it clear.
-My friends already planned to sit here.

425
00:30:39,360 --> 00:30:43,240
-Don't make me sit alone in a cheap seat.
-Don't give me that look.

426
00:30:43,320 --> 00:30:44,960
-Please, buy me the ticket.
-Orn.

427
00:30:45,560 --> 00:30:47,080
What ticket? Where are you going?

428
00:30:47,640 --> 00:30:50,360
What else but a concert ticket?

429
00:30:51,400 --> 00:30:55,200
Well, my favorite K-Pop band's
coming to Thailand for a concert.

430
00:30:55,280 --> 00:30:58,520
I've already saved up 5,000.
I'm asking Mom for 20,000 more.

431
00:30:58,600 --> 00:30:59,880
-What?
-What?

432
00:30:59,960 --> 00:31:02,680
Twenty-five thousand a ticket?

433
00:31:02,760 --> 00:31:04,400
That's my whole month's salary!

434
00:31:04,480 --> 00:31:05,680
Geez.

435
00:31:05,760 --> 00:31:08,520
Don't ask if you can't give me the money.

436
00:31:09,400 --> 00:31:11,440
Come on, dear.

437
00:31:11,520 --> 00:31:15,200
Don't ask your sister for money.
She's working hard to pay off our debts.

438
00:31:15,960 --> 00:31:19,160
I'll just borrow some from Sa-Ang.

439
00:31:19,240 --> 00:31:21,080
Stop it right there, Mom.

440
00:31:21,160 --> 00:31:23,440
We still have our old debts,
and you're adding more?

441
00:31:24,440 --> 00:31:28,360
Orn, there's nothing wrong
with getting the cheapest ticket.

442
00:31:28,440 --> 00:31:31,200
No way. It's embarrassing.

443
00:31:31,280 --> 00:31:33,960
-Oh? Just don't go then.
-Back off.

444
00:31:36,080 --> 00:31:37,480
Come on, Mom.

445
00:31:37,560 --> 00:31:41,320
I'll be frugal after this.
I won't ask for anything else ever again.

446
00:31:41,400 --> 00:31:43,640
-Please.
-Okay, I'll talk to Sa-Ang.

447
00:31:43,720 --> 00:31:45,320
I can pay her back in installments.

448
00:31:45,400 --> 00:31:48,840
-And where are you gonna get that money?
-Yeah, yeah. I'll find a way!

449
00:31:48,920 --> 00:31:51,000
If your "way"
is to keep borrowing from others,

450
00:31:51,080 --> 00:31:52,920
that's still adding more to our debts.

451
00:31:53,000 --> 00:31:53,840
Look.

452
00:31:53,920 --> 00:31:57,200
Ob's already getting his buffalo back.
Of course I gotta give Orn something.

453
00:31:57,280 --> 00:31:58,880
This is not about favoritism.

454
00:32:02,480 --> 00:32:03,400
Orn.

455
00:32:04,240 --> 00:32:06,320
I do want you to go to the concert.

456
00:32:06,960 --> 00:32:10,280
But right now, please understand
that our family is in debt.

457
00:32:10,360 --> 00:32:12,920
We can't spend the way we used to.

458
00:32:13,000 --> 00:32:15,280
All you talk about is debt. Boring!

459
00:32:15,800 --> 00:32:16,960
Orn.

460
00:32:17,880 --> 00:32:19,120
Orn!

461
00:32:22,760 --> 00:32:23,920
Unbelievable.

462
00:32:24,440 --> 00:32:26,000
Have some empathy for her.

463
00:32:34,920 --> 00:32:35,800
Ouch!

464
00:32:36,520 --> 00:32:37,600
Auem?

465
00:32:38,800 --> 00:32:39,720
Your hand hurts?

466
00:32:41,160 --> 00:32:42,880
Yeah, just a little.

467
00:32:43,480 --> 00:32:44,840
Why don't you take a rest?

468
00:32:45,960 --> 00:32:46,840
Leave this to me.

469
00:32:47,440 --> 00:32:50,720
Nah. We can finish sooner if I help out.

470
00:32:52,200 --> 00:32:54,080
Your job at the store starts next week.

471
00:32:54,680 --> 00:32:58,040
And you still have video editing,
grass cutting, and dung scooping to do.

472
00:32:58,120 --> 00:32:59,120
Sure you can do it all?

473
00:33:00,640 --> 00:33:03,760
Dad used to do all that by himself.

474
00:33:03,840 --> 00:33:05,040
Why couldn't I?

475
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:09,320
Am I a burden to you?

476
00:33:15,440 --> 00:33:17,520
Come on, don't think like that.

477
00:33:18,600 --> 00:33:21,480
Come on, help me out. We're almost done.

478
00:33:30,560 --> 00:33:34,160
UTHAI THANI PROVINCE

479
00:33:43,600 --> 00:33:44,600
Hom Thong.

480
00:33:45,480 --> 00:33:47,640
I brought you some bananas
from Dad's trees.

481
00:33:49,720 --> 00:33:51,920
Eat up and feel better soon.

482
00:33:53,040 --> 00:33:54,240
Eat up.

483
00:33:58,360 --> 00:34:00,600
What about Por Chang's semen?

484
00:34:00,680 --> 00:34:02,880
-Have you got someone to do it?
-Not yet, Sia Aun.

485
00:34:03,640 --> 00:34:05,160
Tik knows all of our guys,

486
00:34:05,840 --> 00:34:07,320
so I'm still looking for someone.

487
00:34:10,040 --> 00:34:13,639
Hom Thong's been eating a lot more
since you started helping around here.

488
00:34:16,199 --> 00:34:19,600
Uh, have you and your sister figured out

489
00:34:19,679 --> 00:34:22,159
how to get one million in six months?

490
00:34:22,239 --> 00:34:23,639
That's a lot of money.

491
00:34:26,199 --> 00:34:27,800
I'll do everything to get that money

492
00:34:28,560 --> 00:34:29,679
and bring him home.

493
00:34:31,080 --> 00:34:34,280
How about this? I got a job for you.

494
00:34:34,360 --> 00:34:37,639
So you'll have some money
to help your sister buy Hom Thong back.

495
00:34:37,719 --> 00:34:39,199
I'll give you 50,000.

496
00:34:41,760 --> 00:34:42,760
-Wait, 50,000?
-Yeah.

497
00:34:43,639 --> 00:34:44,639
What kind of job?

498
00:34:49,800 --> 00:34:54,920
POR CHANG
THE MILLION-BAHT STUD BULL

499
00:35:03,760 --> 00:35:06,880
So this is Uncle Tik's home?
The owner of Por Chang?

500
00:35:06,960 --> 00:35:07,800
Yes.

501
00:35:08,440 --> 00:35:11,880
Why don't you just buy the buffalo's semen
from him like everybody else?

502
00:35:12,400 --> 00:35:13,800
Well, he won't sell it to me.

503
00:35:15,160 --> 00:35:19,360
You know, Por Chang's actually
one of Sia Aun's buffaloes.

504
00:35:19,880 --> 00:35:22,640
But one day, he was gone.

505
00:35:23,360 --> 00:35:25,040
Then he showed up here at Tik's.

506
00:35:25,960 --> 00:35:30,120
He insisted that Por Chang's his.
Sia Aun couldn't prove it then,

507
00:35:30,200 --> 00:35:31,600
so he let him keep the buffalo.

508
00:35:33,000 --> 00:35:35,400
-Really?
-Really.

509
00:35:35,480 --> 00:35:37,600
Sia Aun did try to buy him back.

510
00:35:37,680 --> 00:35:39,520
But Tik wouldn't sell him.

511
00:35:40,680 --> 00:35:43,760
I guess he knows that my boss
only breeds good bloodlines.

512
00:35:43,840 --> 00:35:45,360
So he wants to keep Por Chang.

513
00:35:45,440 --> 00:35:49,560
Look. If you pull this off,

514
00:35:49,640 --> 00:35:53,080
Sia Aun might feel generous enough
to lower Hom Thong's price

515
00:35:53,160 --> 00:35:56,320
to just one million,
on top of paying you 50,000.

516
00:35:57,600 --> 00:35:59,800
Well, I'll do it then.

517
00:35:59,880 --> 00:36:02,200
But don't tell me that's Por Chang?

518
00:36:02,280 --> 00:36:04,520
That's him right there.

519
00:36:05,080 --> 00:36:07,840
He's gigantic.
How am I gonna get him out here?

520
00:36:15,640 --> 00:36:16,560
Who's there?

521
00:36:34,120 --> 00:36:37,160
So? Did he agree to it?

522
00:36:38,080 --> 00:36:40,720
He did. And he really bought it

523
00:36:41,400 --> 00:36:44,440
when I told him that Por Chang was yours.

524
00:36:45,240 --> 00:36:47,560
I told him to get close to Tik

525
00:36:48,280 --> 00:36:50,360
to gain his trust.

526
00:36:51,040 --> 00:36:52,560
This better work out

527
00:36:55,240 --> 00:36:57,320
so Por Chang's semen will finally be mine.

528
00:37:02,800 --> 00:37:03,960
Hello.

529
00:37:04,040 --> 00:37:07,720
Today, I'll be teaching you
how to clean a buffalo pen.

530
00:37:07,800 --> 00:37:11,200
Din, our handsome guy, is also with us.

531
00:37:11,280 --> 00:37:13,840
He's helping us clean the pen today.

532
00:37:14,480 --> 00:37:17,440
So, what's the first thing to do?

533
00:37:17,520 --> 00:37:19,240
The first thing to do

534
00:37:19,320 --> 00:37:23,120
is to take Hom Ngern out of her pen.
Come on, girl.

535
00:37:29,640 --> 00:37:31,840
-Alright, okay.
-Here.

536
00:37:33,160 --> 00:37:35,600
Next, we're going to clean inside her pen.

537
00:37:36,160 --> 00:37:38,520
Just keep sweeping. Keep sweeping.

538
00:37:38,600 --> 00:37:40,520
Clean it up like this, right?

539
00:37:44,800 --> 00:37:45,600
CHOK CHAROENSUK FARM

540
00:37:47,880 --> 00:37:48,760
What's this?

541
00:37:54,240 --> 00:37:57,680
Hey, isn't this keychain
from Chok Charoensuk Farm?

542
00:37:57,760 --> 00:37:58,720
Sia Aun's farm.

543
00:37:59,480 --> 00:38:00,600
What is it doing here?

544
00:38:06,960 --> 00:38:09,760
Khwan, here's the new keychain
you asked me to get.

545
00:38:10,360 --> 00:38:11,920
CHOK CHAROENSUK FARM

546
00:38:12,000 --> 00:38:12,920
Thanks.

547
00:38:13,560 --> 00:38:15,680
What happened to the old one?

548
00:38:16,280 --> 00:38:18,680
I don't know.
Must've dropped it somewhere.

549
00:38:24,720 --> 00:38:28,200
I asked everyone at home.
Nobody's ever had this kind of keychain.

550
00:38:30,200 --> 00:38:34,280
If it's not ours,
then someone else must've dropped it.

551
00:38:34,360 --> 00:38:37,440
You mean someone sneaked
into Hom Thong's pen?

552
00:38:38,600 --> 00:38:40,000
Who could it be?

553
00:38:41,640 --> 00:38:45,320
This keychain is a souvenir
from Sia Aun's farm store.

554
00:38:45,400 --> 00:38:46,800
Anybody could've got one.

555
00:38:47,960 --> 00:38:49,920
But Dad,

556
00:38:51,400 --> 00:38:53,280
the red mark on the back looks like blood.

557
00:38:55,200 --> 00:38:56,920
Should we get it tested?

558
00:38:57,000 --> 00:39:00,000
See if this is human blood or something.

559
00:40:38,520 --> 00:40:39,640
Subtitle translation by:
Narawan Promprakai
